# Failed / aborted experiments (commands + observed errors)

## 1. dmwrite/dmread without matrix address -> assembler crash (not an ISA limit)
$ printf 'dmread $lx $lr16v\n' | assemble3 --instruction-mode flat
  terminate called after throwing an instance of 'std::bad_optional_access'
  # cause: dmread grammar is `dmread $l(x|y)<addr> <dst>`; `$lx` is missing <addr>.
  # with `$lx0` it assembles (j=1) and co-issues: see logs/e3_mread.log

## 2. MV sharing a PE line
$ printf 'lpassa $lm0v $ln0v;mvp/n64 $p0@0 $d0@0\n' | assemble3
  Non PE operation after separator.  (ParseError, rc=-6)
  # MV is always its own word.

## 3. Three MAU groups on one line
$ printf 'fvpassa $ls16v $ls24v;fmwrite $ls16v $ly0;fmread $lx0 $lr16v\n' | assemble3
  Instruction field conflict detected between `mau+mwrite` and `mread`.
  # at most 2 of {mau-calc, mau-mwrite, mau-mread} per step

## 4. Different MAU precisions on one line
$ ... 'dvpassa $ls16v $ls24v;gmwrite ...'
  Instruction field conflict detected between `mau_dmode` and `mau_dmode`.
  # the two co-issued MAU groups must use the same precision

## 5. imm with LM0 access
$ printf 'imm i"7" $r16;lpassa $lm0v $ln0v\n' | assemble3
  Instruction field conflict detected between `alu` and `alu`.   # imm is ALU group
$ printf 'imm i"7" $r16;dvpassa $lm0v $ln8v\n' | assemble3
  Instruction field conflict detected between `immediate` and `lm0`.  # bit sharing

## 6. mvn128 is not a mnemonic
$ printf 'mvn128/n64 $p0@0 $d0@0\n' | assemble3
  No valid operation in this line.

## 7. PDM debug get with no preceding MV
$ gpfn3_package_main -i (mvnop; d get $p0n0 4) -d out --offchip-memory-init unique
  Segmentation fault (core dumped)
  # not pursued; PDM contents were probed indirectly through mvp PDM->DRAM instead.
